<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="54cf84bd">The Development Teams includes all of the roles required for development, however the tasks for developing functionality or
features will&amp;nbsp;be assigned to&amp;nbsp;more specific roles within the method based on&amp;nbsp;the required skills.</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="2aca15f1"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="16989188"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="339d873b">&lt;p&gt;
    The Development Team is responsible for:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Developing functionality or features that meet the defined quality conditions
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Self-organizing themselves to complete the work
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Estimating the work effort
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determining and setting capacity
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Defining the quality conditions (i.e., Definition of Done)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Participating in recurring team meetings (e.g., daily scrum)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reviewing product features&amp;nbsp;as defined/requested by stakeholders (typically&amp;nbsp;via the&amp;nbsp;Product Owner as
        representative of the stakeholders)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Contributing to sprint reviews and retrospectives
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Considering product and process improvements throughout the course of the project
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
